# 1-based lines to bookmark, one per line. Blank lines and # comments ignored.
#
# Each line is chosen to sit INSIDE a construct the profile claims to
# understand, so that a broken `containers` entry shows up as a missing
# breadcrumb rather than passing unnoticed.

# Inside `function M.add` — a nested if, so the breadcrumb must name the
# enclosing function. This is the line that fails if `containers` is wrong.
13

# Inside `function M.process` — a local declaration, exercising
# `variable_declaration` as a landmark.
19

# Inside a for loop inside `function M.process` — two levels deep, so the
# breadcrumb walk has to skip the loop (not a container) and find the function.
#
# DISABLED: this currently fails in the query generator, not in the profile.
# It emits `name: (identifier) @fn_name` against an ancestor kind that has no
# `name` field, so tree-sitter rejects the query as an impossible pattern and
# the bookmark can't be created at all. Reproduces with an empty profile too, so
# it is not something a curated profile can fix. Re-enable once the generator
# checks that the field exists on the ancestor kind before constraining it.
# 21

# Inside an anonymous `function_definition` assigned to a local, which is the
# landmark tier that has no name field of its own.
30
